## Composable Patterns

### Reactive Parameters
Many composables accept `MaybeRefOrGetter<T>` for flexibility:
```typescript
function useClipActions(clip: MaybeRefOrGetter<Clip>) {
  const clipValue = () => toValue(clip);
  // Can pass Ref<Clip>, ComputedRef<Clip>, or Clip directly
}
```

### Lifecycle Management
Composables handle their own lifecycle:
```typescript
onMounted(() => {
  // Setup
});

onBeforeUnmount(() => {
  // Cleanup
});
```

### Error Handling
Most composables handle errors internally:
```typescript
try {
  await operation();
  toastStore.success('Done');
} catch (error) {
  console.error(error);
  toastStore.error('Failed');
}
```

### Loading States
Composables expose loading states:
```typescript
const { loading } = useStats();
// Use in template: v-if="loading"
```

